2e785632863f043a985f7953775b6aca191f1169:corpus/QUALITY.md:143:- **Row 79 added after round 48 (a predicate must read the candidate it claims to score, and its battery must exercise a green candidate).** A parser that reads an adjacent evidence cell instead of the score cell can leave its clause green over zero inputs (round-48 A1, `controls/ctl-c2-a1-before.json`); a census comparison between unlike types is permanently false (A3); a battery whose helper set omits the census paths scores the genuine block red (A5/A6); and a mutation that changes an out-of-window quote or appends a second corrections heading is a no-op on a green card (A7/A8). Before freezing, run the proposed instrument against one complete green candidate and each forgery, and inspect the exact field each clause reads. Evidence: `corpus/lessons/round-48.md` `## Mistakes` and `plans/round-48-claims.md` freeze amendments A1–A8.
